.Dd September 12, 2026
.Dt INTEL_PMC 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm intel_pmc
.Nd Intel Power Management Controller driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "device intel_pmc"
.Pp
Alternatively, to load the driver as a
module at boot time, place the following line in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
intel_pmc_load="YES"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver exposes sleep state residency counters and Latency Tolerance
Reporting (LTR) status for Intel Power Management Controllers via
.Xr sysctl 8 .
.Pp
The driver supports debugging S0ix (Modern Standby) power states by
providing the cumulative time the system has spent in S0ix and
identifying which IP blocks are preventing deeper sleep states.
.Pp
On Meteor Lake the package has two PMCs.
The SoC die PMC owns the SLP_S0 residency counter and the LTR state of
the SoC die's IP blocks.
The IO Expander die PMC covers the PCIe Gen5 and Thunderbolt root ports
that live on that die and is hidden from PCI enumeration.
The driver locates both through the Shared SRAM device and exposes the
IOE PMC under the
.Va ioe
sysctl node.
.Pp
If firmware has locked access to the PMC registers, the driver detects
this condition at attach time and reports it via the
.Va access_denied
sysctl.
Register accesses return
.Er EACCES
when access is denied.
.Sh HARDWARE
The following Intel Power Management Controllers are supported by the
.Nm
driver:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Intel Sunrise Point-LP PMC (6th/7th Gen Core mobile, PCI ID 0x8086:0x9d21)
.It
Intel Sunrise Point-H PMC (6th/7th Gen Core desktop/server,
PCI ID 0x8086:0xa121)
.It
Intel Meteor Lake-P/H SoC PMC (PCI ID 0x8086:0x7e7f), and the
Meteor Lake IO Expander PMC (0x7ecf or 0x7ebf) reached through it
.El
.Sh SYSCTLS
The following
.Xr sysctl 8
variables are available.
On Meteor Lake the same set, except
.Va slp_s0_residency ,
is also available under
.Va dev.intel_pmc.%d.ioe
for the IO Expander PMC.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va dev.intel_pmc.%d.access_denied
Set to 1 if firmware has denied access to PMC registers.
.It Va dev.intel_pmc.%d.devid
PCI device ID of this PMC.
.It Va dev.intel_pmc.%d.pwrm_base
Physical address of the PMC's PWRM register block.
.It Va dev.intel_pmc.%d.ltr_ignore
Latency Tolerance Reporting (LTR) ignore mask.
Each bit corresponds to one IP block, in the order printed by
.Va ltr .
Setting a bit tells the PMC to ignore that IP's LTR requirements,
allowing S0ix entry even if the IP would otherwise block it.
A clear bit means the IP's requirements are considered and can
prevent S0ix.
Bits above the number of IP blocks for the platform are masked off.
.Pp
Sunrise Point has 17 ignorable IP blocks, the Meteor Lake SoC PMC 26,
and the Meteor Lake IOE PMC 24.
.It Va dev.intel_pmc.%d.ltr
One line per IP block: its index (the bit number in
.Va ltr_ignore ) ,
name, raw LTR register value, the decoded snoop and non-snoop latency
tolerance in nanoseconds, and whether it is currently ignored.
The final two entries, CURRENT_PLATFORM and AGGREGATED_SYSTEM, report
the PMC's own aggregate and cannot be ignored.
An IP reporting a small tolerance is what prevents the platform from
entering S0ix.
.It Va dev.intel_pmc.%d.slp_s0_residency
Cumulative time in microseconds that the PCH has been in the deepest
S0ix state.
The counter tick is 104\ us on Sunrise Point and 122\ us on Meteor Lake.
The PCH enters this state when the CPU is in Package C10, the PCH is in
low power mode, ModPhy lanes are power-gated, and PLLs are idle.
A value that never advances indicates S0ix transitions are not occurring.
.Pp
The counter is 32-bit.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr acpi 4 ,
.Xr pci 4 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Pp
Intel 100 Series Chipset Family PCH Datasheet, Volume 2, Section 4.3.
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Abdelkader Boudih Aq Mt freebsd@seuros.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Other PCH generations (Cannon Point, Tiger Lake, etc.) have different
register layouts and are not handled by this driver.
